[00:03.35]DANCE (AROUND)
[00:19.14]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[00:24.97]Free as a man , one day left before the gate turns
[00:30.31]Light as the wind that dances through the jail's trees
[00:35.18]Or the ropes of a ring that dance beneath the blow
[00:42.20]Dance as long as you can dance, on the canvas, on the tar
[00:45.07]On a burnt ground, in the shadow of a master
[00:49.70]Come, let yourself be carried by every kind of music
[00:54.57]Rising from a speaker or a kids playing bow.
[01:01.19]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[01:06.30]Dance in the arms of your moher, or Norah and Jo.
[01:11.56]Dance to find love again, and madness too
[01:16.83]Dance to dazzle your soul when it’s bored and blue
[01:43.48]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[01:48.19]So you no longer carry the count and the trials on your back
[01:50.98]And you will see in plain sight, summer burst through the light
[01:53.93]pray fir torrents of joy running loose under your skin
[01:59.28]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[02:01.83]Dance so a brand-new day may bloom behind the wall
[02:09.65]Dance the way we fight, dance the way we love
[02:14.91]Dance the way we write our names upon the walls
[02:20.34]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[02:25.69]Dance as long as you can dance. Come,
[02:25.69]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[02:29.36]the round is open!
[02:30.95]Dance as long as you can dance, dance around the earth
[02:36.22]Dance as long as you can dance. Come, the round is open!
